cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Certified worst-case intervals with a matched permutation null for spatial
  co-expression contrasts under molecule reassignment
message: >-
  If you use this code or the certified-interval construction, please cite the
  accompanying manuscript and this repository.
authors:
  - given-names: Amy
    family-names: Wang
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-22"
repository-code: "https://github.com/amywang2010/lr-certificates"
abstract: >-
  Per-contrast intervals for co-expression scores in spatial transcriptomics,
  valid over a declared set of molecule-to-cell reassignments (boundary-local
  reassignment with capacity constraints, mask erosion/dilation, and a
  parameterised donor radius), with a permutation null that recomputes the
  worst-case object under each label permutation. Certification is reported in
  two layers, interval sign and claim status. Evaluated on three public Xenium
  sections spanning two panel densities and two tumor types.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - co-expression
  - molecule reassignment
  - certified intervals
  - matched permutation null
